Subject: Add an opt-in PQ3 128-value CPU format/reference, with inference disabled
Base: llama.cpp a34de8618b25dfc32ee43749db47d767a9f0a25d (b12015), after 0003-0007
Donor: tetherto/qvac-fabric-llm.cpp PR 115, head 362003a25376555e5c01939ed82710bbb2c3bcf8
License: MIT, Copyright (c) 2023-2024 The ggml authors; upstream LICENSE retained

Why: the pin has rotation but no codebook KV format. Establish a deterministic
CPU oracle before graph/Vulkan integration. Append type 44; preserve IDs 0-43.
PQ3 stores 48 packed index bytes then a half L2 norm (50 bytes / 128 values).
Keep donor codebook/packing, omit its mutable norm-policy/environment and sign
initialization. Row functions accept already transformed coordinates. Canonicalize
FP16 norm underflow to zero; guarded project shims reject nonfinite/oversized norms.
No llama_context_params layout changes. ggml_pq3_reference_abi_v1 binds the layout.
Cache selection and PQ3 model weights/quantization fail closed in this phase.
Tests: test-pq3-reference (model/GPU independent), plus guarded Rust codec tests.
The project feature stages this patch; no runtime CLI cache option is introduced.

